        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "c66986b8f4eb4f4eb8fcee9c29391198618a52f763038f31d9aab2cf23d724c6",
        "target": "Last year, Jessica's monthly expenses were:\n- Rent: $1000\n- Food: $200\n- Car insurance: $100\n\nTotal monthly expenses last year: $1000 + $200 + $100 = $1300\n\nThis year, the expenses are:\n- Rent: $1000 * 1.30 = $1300 (30% increase)\n- Food: $200 * 1.50 = $300 (50% increase)\n- Car insurance: $100 * 3 = $300 (triples)\n\nTotal monthly expenses this year: $1300 + $300 + $300 = $1900\n\nThe increase in monthly expenses is: $1900 - $1300 = $600\n\nOver the whole year, the increase is: $600 * 12 = $7200\n\nFINAL: 7200",
