        "target": "Given the problem, I identified the following quantities:\n- Last year's monthly rent: $1000\n- Last year's monthly food cost: $200\n- Last year's monthly car insurance cost: $100\n\nThe unknown I needed to find was the total additional amount Jessica pays over the whole year compared to last year.\n\nTo solve this, I first calculated the total monthly expenses for last year:\n\\[ 1000 + 200 + 100 = 1300 \\]\n\nNext, I calculated the new monthly expenses for this year:\n- New rent: \\( 1000 \\times 1.30 = 1300 \\)\n- New food cost: \\( 200 \\times 1.50 = 300 \\)\n- New car insurance cost: \\( 100 \\times 3 = 300 \\)\n\nSo, the total monthly expenses for this year are:\n\\[ 1300 + 300 + 300 = 1900 \\]\n\nThe increase in monthly expenses is:\n\\[ 1900 - 1300 = 600 \\]\n\nTo find the total increase over the whole year, I multiplied the monthly increase by 12:\n\\[ 600 \\times 12 = 7200 \\]\n\nI checked this result by ensuring that the operations were correctly applied and the arithmetic was accurate. The final answer matches the problem statement.\n\nFINAL: 7200",
